 {"name": "A scandal of particularity", "who": "Critics from the Enlightenment on, such as Voltaire", "view": "A universal God would not reveal himself to one small people in one corner of the world.", "evidence": "The rest of humanity seems left out for two thousand years."},
 {"name": "God works through the particular", "who": "Many modern theologians", "view": "Love is always particular: God reaches the world as people do, through one family, one place, one person.", "evidence": "The incarnation: God in one man, in one time and place."}
